# Names only; no credentials. Backend reads process environment variables.
# No automatic .env loading. Export values in your shell or inject them at runtime.
# FLASK_DEBUG: blank/0/false disables debug; 1/true enables local debug only.
# BACKEND_PORT: blank defaults to 5000; otherwise use 1-65535.
# SECRET_KEY: optional Flask session secret; JWT never uses it as a fallback.
# JWT_SECRET_KEY: independent random signing secret, at least 32 bytes; no fallback.
# JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECONDS: blank defaults to 900; integer 60-86400.
# DATABASE_URL: blank disables database initialization; migrations require a URL.
# Drivers: mysql+pymysql (application target), sqlite (isolated development/tests).
# SQLite must use :memory: or an absolute file path. See docs/setup/database-foundation.md.
FLASK_DEBUG=
SECRET_KEY=
JWT_SECRET_KEY=
JWT_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECONDS=
DATABASE_URL=
BACKEND_PORT=
FRONTEND_PORT=
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
V17_ARTIFACT_DIR=
